A||||6||Gold87SE||What to do?||||1||
Z||000000||Gold87SE||09-17-2000||10:03 PM||||My 2.8 is pretty much done. It has a horrendous rod knock. What do you guys think would be the best thing for me to do? Another 2.8? A 3.1 Conversion? A 3.4 conversion? A 350? Anything else? I don't know if it would  be worth it getting my 2.8 repaired.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Xtreme Fiero's||09-17-2000||10:16 PM||||If I was in your shoes I'd go for the 3.1/3.2. just rebuild the old 2.8 get a high performance cam and some foraged pistons. but if you want an ass load of power I'd look into a LPE 383 LT1  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> youk know with the 1000 CFM throttle body and accell ECM and a SLP intake &  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> make yourself a Firehawk Fiero GT ||||reg||14
Z||000002||Cooter||09-17-2000||10:43 PM||||I have a 3.4 that I bought used in my GT. It is a very good performing engine-when I get to drive it. Too much to do, too little time for fun  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||09-17-2000||10:53 PM||||I suspect you'll get a variety of answers on this one. Some will say go w/ the larger engines, for performance sake and for bragging rights. Thats perfectly alright.<BR>I however, am somewhat of a purist (to an extent). I would personally either rebuild the 2.8, or get another Fiero 2.8 engine.<BR>I say this for several reasons. <BR>In my opinion the 2.8 is plenty fast enough...how fast do you really need to go anyway? Besides, if you have to have more power, there are always options for the 2.8..nitrous, turbo, most any add on.<BR>Also, by replacing your Fiero engine w/ another, you open up a whole new can of worms. If you ever encounter a problem, forget going to Autozone (or wherever) and saying "do you have a pick up coil for a 2.8 Fiero V6 distributor?"...because, obviously, you dont have a Fiero engine. This dosnt even include the entire installation project of putting an engine designed to go into another car into a Fiero.<BR>I suspect the GM engineers knew what they were doing when they put the 2.8 in there.<BR>Just my 2 cents worth.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||09-17-2000||11:03 PM||||How much money do you want to spend or have to spend?  How much time do you have to repair the car?  Will you do this yourself or have some one else do the work?  Is the car primary transportation or for pleasure?<P>Worse case senerio: the Fiero is primary vehicle, you have no money, no engine rebuild experience and need the car next week.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Rebuild kits for a 2.8 ARE $350.<P>To get a rebuilt or new complete engine $1000-3000 (depending on engine).  Replacement by automotive technician $1000-2000.  Time ?40 hours.  Other fixes while the engine is out bushings, water pump, injectors, exhaust mainifold clean and polish,(replace probably cracked) intake manifold clean and polish, transmission overhaul? Just as well, the engine is out.<BR>Upgrade suspension needed for bigger engines.<P>A 3800 S/C swap including a decent engine is under $10000. A 3.4 swap is $4000.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>You can do what ever your wallet says you can do.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000005||Gold87SE||09-18-2000||01:06 AM||||Well, my wallet tells me to go with the 2.8 rebuild.||||reg||1
Z||000006||ThatRickGuy||09-18-2000||10:14 AM||||I'm on a 3.1 conversion, I was in a similar boat, 2.8 had a nasty knock (started 3 days after I bought it!!!) The conversion isn't much more then a 2.8 professional rebuild. With a complete pro job, balancing and 6 connecting rods (yes, all 6 were bad!) total bill came out to $1800. that's including crank, cam, lifters, springs, gaskets, and for labor, disassembly, hot tank, valve guides, 3 angle valve job, .020 cylinder bore, balance, etc. and complete re-assembly. after all that, I'm looking at about 165 hp and 200 ft/lbs torque.||||reg||1
